{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Ollama adapter provides access to local models running via Ollama, allowing you to run AI models on your own infrastructure with full privacy and no API costs."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-ollama\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-ollama\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-ollama\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-ollama\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-ollama\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-ollama\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-ollama\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-ollama\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Usage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollamaText } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: ollamaText(\"llama3\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage-custom-host","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Usage - Custom Host"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createOllamaChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst adapter = createOllamaChat(\"llama3\", \"http://your-server:11434\");\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter,\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createOllamaChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\n// Custom host (URL string)\nconst adapter = createOllamaChat(\"llama3\", \"http://your-server:11434\");\n\n// Custom client config (e.g., custom headers, fetch)\nconst adapter2 = createOllamaChat(\"llama3\", {\n  host: \"http://your-server:11434\",\n  headers: { Authorization: \"Bearer ...\" },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"behind-a-proxy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behind a proxy"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Route every request through a gateway, such as Cloudflare AI Gateway or a corporate proxy, with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseURL"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultHeaders"},{"type":"text","value":". These two option names are the same on every TanStack AI adapter, so one gateway config works for all of them."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createOllamaChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst adapter = createOllamaChat(\"llama3\", {\n  baseURL: \"https://gateway.example.com/ollama\",\n  defaultHeaders: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.GATEWAY_TOKEN}` },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"host"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"headers"},{"type":"text","value":" are aliases of the same two options. If you set both forms, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseURL"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultHeaders"},{"type":"text","value":" win."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"available-models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available Models"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To see available models on your Ollama instance:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"ollama list","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"popular-models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Popular Models"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"llama3"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"llama3.1"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"llama3.2"},{"type":"text","value":" - Meta's Llama models"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mistral"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mistral:7b"},{"type":"text","value":" - Mistral AI models"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mixtral"},{"type":"text","value":" - Mixtral MoE model"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codellama"},{"type":"text","value":" - Code-focused Llama"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"phi3"},{"type":"text","value":" - Microsoft's Phi models"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemma"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemma2"},{"type":"text","value":" - Google's Gemma models"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"qwen2"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"qwen2.5"},{"type":"text","value":" - Alibaba's Qwen models"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"deepseek-coder"},{"type":"text","value":" - DeepSeek coding model"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example-chat-completion","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example: Chat Completion"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollamaText } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: ollamaText(\"llama3\"),\n    messages,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example-with-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example: With Tools"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse, toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollamaText } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst getLocalDataDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"get_local_data\",\n  description: \"Get data from local storage\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    key: z.string(),\n  }),\n});\n\nconst getLocalData = getLocalDataDef.server(async ({ key }) => {\n  // Access local data\n  return { data: \"...\" };\n});\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: ollamaText(\"llama3\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [getLocalData],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Tool support varies by model. Models like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"llama3"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mistral"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"qwen2"},{"type":"text","value":" generally have good tool calling support."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ollama supports various provider-specific options. Unlike the other providers, Ollama nests its sampling and runner parameters inside an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":" object "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"within"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"top_p"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"num_predict"},{"type":"text","value":" (the token-limit key) all live under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.options"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollamaText } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: ollamaText(\"llama3:latest\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n  modelOptions: {\n    options: {\n      temperature: 0.7,\n      top_p: 0.9,\n      top_k: 40,\n      num_predict: 1000, // Max tokens to generate\n      repeat_penalty: 1.1,\n      num_ctx: 4096, // Context window size\n      num_gpu: -1, // GPU layers (-1 = auto)\n    },\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you previously passed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"topP"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTokens"},{"type":"text","value":" at the root of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":", note that for Ollama they map to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.options.temperature"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.options.top_p"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.options.num_predict"},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"../migration/sampling-options-to-model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"advanced-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Advanced Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All sampling and runner parameters are nested under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.options"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"modelOptions: {\n  options: {\n    // Sampling\n    temperature: 0.7,\n    top_p: 0.9,\n    top_k: 40,\n    min_p: 0.05,\n    typical_p: 1.0,\n\n    // Generation\n    num_predict: 1000,\n    repeat_penalty: 1.1,\n    repeat_last_n: 64,\n    penalize_newline: false,\n\n    // Performance\n    num_ctx: 4096,\n    num_batch: 512,\n    num_gpu: -1,\n    num_thread: 0, // 0 = auto\n\n    // Memory\n    use_mmap: true,\n    use_mlock: false,\n\n    // Mirostat sampling\n    mirostat: 0, // 0 = disabled, 1 = Mirostat, 2 = Mirostat 2.0\n    mirostat_tau: 5.0,\n    mirostat_eta: 0.1,\n  },\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"summarization","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Summarization"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Summarize long text content locally:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { summarize } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollamaSummarize } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst result = await summarize({\n  adapter: ollamaSummarize(\"llama3\"),\n  text: \"Your long text to summarize...\",\n  maxLength: 100,\n  style: \"concise\", // \"concise\" | \"bullet-points\" | \"paragraph\"\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.summary);","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"embeddings","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Embeddings"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generate embedding vectors locally with any Ollama embedding model:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollamaEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: ollamaEmbedding(\"nomic-embed-text\"),\n  input: [\"a red guitar\", \"a blue drum kit\"],\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.embeddings[0]?.vector);","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Known models ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nomic-embed-text"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mxbai-embed-large"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"all-minilm"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snowflake-arctic-embed"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bge-m3"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"embeddinggemma"},{"type":"text","value":") get autocomplete, and any other model name is accepted. Pull the model first with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ollama pull nomic-embed-text"},{"type":"text","value":". Output dimensions are fixed per model — the top-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dimensions"},{"type":"text","value":" option is not supported."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../embeddings.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Embeddings guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the full API."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"setting-up-ollama","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Setting Up Ollama"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"1-install-ollama","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Install Ollama"}]},{"type":"code","value":"# macOS\nbrew install ollama\n\n# Linux\ncurl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh\n\n# Windows\n# Download from https://ollama.com","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"2-pull-a-model","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Pull a Model"}]},{"type":"code","value":"ollama pull llama3","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"3-start-ollama-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Start Ollama Server"}]},{"type":"code","value":"ollama serve","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server runs on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"http://localhost:11434"},{"type":"text","value":" by default."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"running-on-a-remote-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Running on a Remote Server"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createOllamaChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst adapter = createOllamaChat(\"llama3\", \"http://your-server:11434\");","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To expose Ollama on a network interface:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0:11434 ollama serve","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"environment-variables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variables"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optionally set the host in environment variables:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"api-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API Reference"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"ollamatext-model","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ollamaText(model)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an Ollama text/chat adapter using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OLLAMA_HOST"},{"type":"text","value":" from the environment (defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"http://localhost:11434"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model"},{"type":"text","value":" - Model name (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"llama3\""},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"mistral:7b\""},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createollamachat-model-hostorconfig","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createOllamaChat(model, hostOrConfig?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an Ollama text/chat adapter with an explicit host or client config."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model"},{"type":"text","value":" - Model name"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hostOrConfig?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Either an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OLLAMA_HOST"},{"type":"text","value":"-style URL string, or an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OllamaClientConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" object (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ baseURL, defaultHeaders }"},{"type":"text","value":"). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"host"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"headers"},{"type":"text","value":" are aliases."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"ollamasummarize-model-createollamasummarize-model-hostorconfig","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ollamaSummarize(model)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createOllamaSummarize(model, hostOrConfig?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an Ollama summarization adapter — same signature shape as the chat adapter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"benefits-of-ollama","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Benefits of Ollama"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅ "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Privacy"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Data stays on your infrastructure"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅ "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cost"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - No API costs after hardware"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅ "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Customization"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Use any compatible model"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅ "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Offline"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Works without internet"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅ "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Speed"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - No network latency for local deployment"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"limitations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limitations"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image Generation"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Ollama does not support image generation. Use OpenAI or Gemini for image generation."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Performance"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Depends on your hardware (GPU recommended for larger models)"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../getting-started/quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Getting Started"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Learn the basics"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../tools/tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Learn about tools"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./openai","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other Adapters"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Explore other providers"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic Usage","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage-custom-host","text":"Basic Usage - Custom Host","level":2},{"id":"configuration","text":"Configuration","level":2},{"id":"behind-a-proxy","text":"Behind a proxy","level":2},{"id":"available-models","text":"Available Models","level":2},{"id":"popular-models","text":"Popular Models","level":3},{"id":"example-chat-completion","text":"Example: Chat Completion","level":2},{"id":"example-with-tools","text":"Example: With Tools","level":2},{"id":"model-options","text":"Model Options","level":2},{"id":"advanced-options","text":"Advanced Options","level":3},{"id":"summarization","text":"Summarization","level":2},{"id":"embeddings","text":"Embeddings","level":2},{"id":"setting-up-ollama","text":"Setting Up Ollama","level":2},{"id":"1-install-ollama","text":"1. Install Ollama","level":3},{"id":"2-pull-a-model","text":"2. Pull a Model","level":3},{"id":"3-start-ollama-server","text":"3. Start Ollama Server","level":3},{"id":"running-on-a-remote-server","text":"Running on a Remote Server","level":2},{"id":"environment-variables","text":"Environment Variables","level":2},{"id":"api-reference","text":"API Reference","level":2},{"id":"ollamatext-model","text":"ollamaText(model)","level":3},{"id":"createollamachat-model-hostorconfig","text":"createOllamaChat(model, hostOrConfig?)","level":3},{"id":"ollamasummarize-model-createollamasummarize-model-hostorconfig","text":"ollamaSummarize(model) / createOllamaSummarize(model, hostOrConfig?)","level":3},{"id":"benefits-of-ollama","text":"Benefits of Ollama","level":2},{"id":"limitations","text":"Limitations","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe Ollama adapter provides access to local models running via Ollama, allowing you to run AI models on your own infrastructure with full privacy and no API costs.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-ollama\nvue: @tanstack/ai-ollama\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-ollama\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-ollama\npreact: @tanstack/ai-ollama\nangular: @tanstack/ai-ollama\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-ollama\noctane: @tanstack/ai-ollama\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollamaText } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: ollamaText(\"llama3\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\n## Basic Usage - Custom Host\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createOllamaChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst adapter = createOllamaChat(\"llama3\", \"http://your-server:11434\");\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter,\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\n```typescript\nimport { createOllamaChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\n// Custom host (URL string)\nconst adapter = createOllamaChat(\"llama3\", \"http://your-server:11434\");\n\n// Custom client config (e.g., custom headers, fetch)\nconst adapter2 = createOllamaChat(\"llama3\", {\n  host: \"http://your-server:11434\",\n  headers: { Authorization: \"Bearer ...\" },\n});\n```\n\n## Behind a proxy\n\nRoute every request through a gateway, such as Cloudflare AI Gateway or a corporate proxy, with `baseURL` and `defaultHeaders`. These two option names are the same on every TanStack AI adapter, so one gateway config works for all of them.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createOllamaChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst adapter = createOllamaChat(\"llama3\", {\n  baseURL: \"https://gateway.example.com/ollama\",\n  defaultHeaders: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.GATEWAY_TOKEN}` },\n});\n```\n\n`host` and `headers` are aliases of the same two options. If you set both forms, `baseURL` and `defaultHeaders` win.\n\n## Available Models\n\nTo see available models on your Ollama instance:\n\n```bash\nollama list\n```\n\n### Popular Models\n\n- `llama3` / `llama3.1` / `llama3.2` - Meta's Llama models\n- `mistral` / `mistral:7b` - Mistral AI models\n- `mixtral` - Mixtral MoE model\n- `codellama` - Code-focused Llama\n- `phi3` - Microsoft's Phi models\n- `gemma` / `gemma2` - Google's Gemma models\n- `qwen2` / `qwen2.5` - Alibaba's Qwen models\n- `deepseek-coder` - DeepSeek coding model\n\n## Example: Chat Completion\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollamaText } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: ollamaText(\"llama3\"),\n    messages,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n## Example: With Tools\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse, toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollamaText } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst getLocalDataDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"get_local_data\",\n  description: \"Get data from local storage\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    key: z.string(),\n  }),\n});\n\nconst getLocalData = getLocalDataDef.server(async ({ key }) => {\n  // Access local data\n  return { data: \"...\" };\n});\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: ollamaText(\"llama3\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [getLocalData],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n**Note:** Tool support varies by model. Models like `llama3`, `mistral`, and `qwen2` generally have good tool calling support.\n\n## Model Options\n\nOllama supports various provider-specific options. Unlike the other providers, Ollama nests its sampling and runner parameters inside an `options` object **within** `modelOptions` — `temperature`, `top_p`, and `num_predict` (the token-limit key) all live under `modelOptions.options`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollamaText } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: ollamaText(\"llama3:latest\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n  modelOptions: {\n    options: {\n      temperature: 0.7,\n      top_p: 0.9,\n      top_k: 40,\n      num_predict: 1000, // Max tokens to generate\n      repeat_penalty: 1.1,\n      num_ctx: 4096, // Context window size\n      num_gpu: -1, // GPU layers (-1 = auto)\n    },\n  },\n});\n```\n\n> If you previously passed `temperature` / `topP` / `maxTokens` at the root of `chat()`, note that for Ollama they map to `modelOptions.options.temperature`, `modelOptions.options.top_p`, and `modelOptions.options.num_predict`. See [Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions](../migration/sampling-options-to-model-options).\n\n### Advanced Options\n\nAll sampling and runner parameters are nested under `modelOptions.options`:\n\n```typescript ignore\nmodelOptions: {\n  options: {\n    // Sampling\n    temperature: 0.7,\n    top_p: 0.9,\n    top_k: 40,\n    min_p: 0.05,\n    typical_p: 1.0,\n\n    // Generation\n    num_predict: 1000,\n    repeat_penalty: 1.1,\n    repeat_last_n: 64,\n    penalize_newline: false,\n\n    // Performance\n    num_ctx: 4096,\n    num_batch: 512,\n    num_gpu: -1,\n    num_thread: 0, // 0 = auto\n\n    // Memory\n    use_mmap: true,\n    use_mlock: false,\n\n    // Mirostat sampling\n    mirostat: 0, // 0 = disabled, 1 = Mirostat, 2 = Mirostat 2.0\n    mirostat_tau: 5.0,\n    mirostat_eta: 0.1,\n  },\n}\n```\n\n## Summarization\n\nSummarize long text content locally:\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { summarize } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollamaSummarize } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst result = await summarize({\n  adapter: ollamaSummarize(\"llama3\"),\n  text: \"Your long text to summarize...\",\n  maxLength: 100,\n  style: \"concise\", // \"concise\" | \"bullet-points\" | \"paragraph\"\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.summary);\n```\n\n## Embeddings\n\nGenerate embedding vectors locally with any Ollama embedding model:\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollamaEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: ollamaEmbedding(\"nomic-embed-text\"),\n  input: [\"a red guitar\", \"a blue drum kit\"],\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.embeddings[0]?.vector);\n```\n\nKnown models (`nomic-embed-text`, `mxbai-embed-large`, `all-minilm`, `snowflake-arctic-embed`, `bge-m3`, `embeddinggemma`) get autocomplete, and any other model name is accepted. Pull the model first with `ollama pull nomic-embed-text`. Output dimensions are fixed per model — the top-level `dimensions` option is not supported.\n\nSee the [Embeddings guide](../embeddings.md) for the full API.\n\n## Setting Up Ollama\n\n### 1. Install Ollama\n\n```bash\n# macOS\nbrew install ollama\n\n# Linux\ncurl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh\n\n# Windows\n# Download from https://ollama.com\n```\n\n### 2. Pull a Model\n\n```bash\nollama pull llama3\n```\n\n### 3. Start Ollama Server\n\n```bash\nollama serve\n```\n\nThe server runs on `http://localhost:11434` by default.\n\n## Running on a Remote Server\n\n```typescript\nimport { createOllamaChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst adapter = createOllamaChat(\"llama3\", \"http://your-server:11434\");\n```\n\nTo expose Ollama on a network interface:\n\n```bash\nOLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0:11434 ollama serve\n```\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nOptionally set the host in environment variables:\n\n```bash\nOLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434\n```\n\n## API Reference\n\n### `ollamaText(model)`\n\nCreates an Ollama text/chat adapter using `OLLAMA_HOST` from the environment (defaults to `http://localhost:11434`).\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- `model` - Model name (e.g. `\"llama3\"`, `\"mistral:7b\"`)\n\n### `createOllamaChat(model, hostOrConfig?)`\n\nCreates an Ollama text/chat adapter with an explicit host or client config.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- `model` - Model name\n- `hostOrConfig?` - Either an `OLLAMA_HOST`-style URL string, or an `OllamaClientConfig` object (e.g. `{ baseURL, defaultHeaders }`). `host` and `headers` are aliases.\n\n### `ollamaSummarize(model)` / `createOllamaSummarize(model, hostOrConfig?)`\n\nCreates an Ollama summarization adapter — same signature shape as the chat adapter.\n\n## Benefits of Ollama\n\n- ✅ **Privacy** - Data stays on your infrastructure\n- ✅ **Cost** - No API costs after hardware\n- ✅ **Customization** - Use any compatible model\n- ✅ **Offline** - Works without internet\n- ✅ **Speed** - No network latency for local deployment\n\n## Limitations\n\n- **Image Generation**: Ollama does not support image generation. Use OpenAI or Gemini for image generation.\n- **Performance**: Depends on your hardware (GPU recommended for larger models)\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Getting Started](../getting-started/quick-start) - Learn the basics\n- [Tools Guide](../tools/tools) - Learn about tools\n- [Other Adapters](./openai) - Explore other providers\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Ollama\nid: ollama-adapter\norder: 4\ndescription: \"Run local LLMs with Ollama in TanStack AI for private, no-cost AI on your own hardware via the @tanstack/ai-ollama adapter.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - ollama\n  - local llm\n  - self-hosted\n  - privacy\n  - llama\n  - offline ai\n  - adapter\n---\n\nThe Ollama adapter provides access to local models running via Ollama, allowing you to run AI models on your own infrastructure with full privacy and no API costs.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-ollama\nvue: @tanstack/ai-ollama\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-ollama\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-ollama\npreact: @tanstack/ai-ollama\nangular: @tanstack/ai-ollama\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-ollama\noctane: @tanstack/ai-ollama\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollamaText } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: ollamaText(\"llama3\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\n## Basic Usage - Custom Host\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createOllamaChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst adapter = createOllamaChat(\"llama3\", \"http://your-server:11434\");\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter,\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\n```typescript\nimport { createOllamaChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\n// Custom host (URL string)\nconst adapter = createOllamaChat(\"llama3\", \"http://your-server:11434\");\n\n// Custom client config (e.g., custom headers, fetch)\nconst adapter2 = createOllamaChat(\"llama3\", {\n  host: \"http://your-server:11434\",\n  headers: { Authorization: \"Bearer ...\" },\n});\n```\n\n## Behind a proxy\n\nRoute every request through a gateway, such as Cloudflare AI Gateway or a corporate proxy, with `baseURL` and `defaultHeaders`. These two option names are the same on every TanStack AI adapter, so one gateway config works for all of them.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createOllamaChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst adapter = createOllamaChat(\"llama3\", {\n  baseURL: \"https://gateway.example.com/ollama\",\n  defaultHeaders: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.GATEWAY_TOKEN}` },\n});\n```\n\n`host` and `headers` are aliases of the same two options. If you set both forms, `baseURL` and `defaultHeaders` win.\n\n## Available Models\n\nTo see available models on your Ollama instance:\n\n```bash\nollama list\n```\n\n### Popular Models\n\n- `llama3` / `llama3.1` / `llama3.2` - Meta's Llama models\n- `mistral` / `mistral:7b` - Mistral AI models\n- `mixtral` - Mixtral MoE model\n- `codellama` - Code-focused Llama\n- `phi3` - Microsoft's Phi models\n- `gemma` / `gemma2` - Google's Gemma models\n- `qwen2` / `qwen2.5` - Alibaba's Qwen models\n- `deepseek-coder` - DeepSeek coding model\n\n## Example: Chat Completion\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollamaText } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: ollamaText(\"llama3\"),\n    messages,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n## Example: With Tools\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse, toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollamaText } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst getLocalDataDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"get_local_data\",\n  description: \"Get data from local storage\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    key: z.string(),\n  }),\n});\n\nconst getLocalData = getLocalDataDef.server(async ({ key }) => {\n  // Access local data\n  return { data: \"...\" };\n});\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: ollamaText(\"llama3\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [getLocalData],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n**Note:** Tool support varies by model. Models like `llama3`, `mistral`, and `qwen2` generally have good tool calling support.\n\n## Model Options\n\nOllama supports various provider-specific options. Unlike the other providers, Ollama nests its sampling and runner parameters inside an `options` object **within** `modelOptions` — `temperature`, `top_p`, and `num_predict` (the token-limit key) all live under `modelOptions.options`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollamaText } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: ollamaText(\"llama3:latest\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n  modelOptions: {\n    options: {\n      temperature: 0.7,\n      top_p: 0.9,\n      top_k: 40,\n      num_predict: 1000, // Max tokens to generate\n      repeat_penalty: 1.1,\n      num_ctx: 4096, // Context window size\n      num_gpu: -1, // GPU layers (-1 = auto)\n    },\n  },\n});\n```\n\n> If you previously passed `temperature` / `topP` / `maxTokens` at the root of `chat()`, note that for Ollama they map to `modelOptions.options.temperature`, `modelOptions.options.top_p`, and `modelOptions.options.num_predict`. See [Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions](../migration/sampling-options-to-model-options).\n\n### Advanced Options\n\nAll sampling and runner parameters are nested under `modelOptions.options`:\n\n```typescript ignore\nmodelOptions: {\n  options: {\n    // Sampling\n    temperature: 0.7,\n    top_p: 0.9,\n    top_k: 40,\n    min_p: 0.05,\n    typical_p: 1.0,\n\n    // Generation\n    num_predict: 1000,\n    repeat_penalty: 1.1,\n    repeat_last_n: 64,\n    penalize_newline: false,\n\n    // Performance\n    num_ctx: 4096,\n    num_batch: 512,\n    num_gpu: -1,\n    num_thread: 0, // 0 = auto\n\n    // Memory\n    use_mmap: true,\n    use_mlock: false,\n\n    // Mirostat sampling\n    mirostat: 0, // 0 = disabled, 1 = Mirostat, 2 = Mirostat 2.0\n    mirostat_tau: 5.0,\n    mirostat_eta: 0.1,\n  },\n}\n```\n\n## Summarization\n\nSummarize long text content locally:\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { summarize } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollamaSummarize } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst result = await summarize({\n  adapter: ollamaSummarize(\"llama3\"),\n  text: \"Your long text to summarize...\",\n  maxLength: 100,\n  style: \"concise\", // \"concise\" | \"bullet-points\" | \"paragraph\"\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.summary);\n```\n\n## Embeddings\n\nGenerate embedding vectors locally with any Ollama embedding model:\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { ollamaEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: ollamaEmbedding(\"nomic-embed-text\"),\n  input: [\"a red guitar\", \"a blue drum kit\"],\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.embeddings[0]?.vector);\n```\n\nKnown models (`nomic-embed-text`, `mxbai-embed-large`, `all-minilm`, `snowflake-arctic-embed`, `bge-m3`, `embeddinggemma`) get autocomplete, and any other model name is accepted. Pull the model first with `ollama pull nomic-embed-text`. Output dimensions are fixed per model — the top-level `dimensions` option is not supported.\n\nSee the [Embeddings guide](../embeddings.md) for the full API.\n\n## Setting Up Ollama\n\n### 1. Install Ollama\n\n```bash\n# macOS\nbrew install ollama\n\n# Linux\ncurl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh\n\n# Windows\n# Download from https://ollama.com\n```\n\n### 2. Pull a Model\n\n```bash\nollama pull llama3\n```\n\n### 3. Start Ollama Server\n\n```bash\nollama serve\n```\n\nThe server runs on `http://localhost:11434` by default.\n\n## Running on a Remote Server\n\n```typescript\nimport { createOllamaChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-ollama\";\n\nconst adapter = createOllamaChat(\"llama3\", \"http://your-server:11434\");\n```\n\nTo expose Ollama on a network interface:\n\n```bash\nOLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0:11434 ollama serve\n```\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nOptionally set the host in environment variables:\n\n```bash\nOLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434\n```\n\n## API Reference\n\n### `ollamaText(model)`\n\nCreates an Ollama text/chat adapter using `OLLAMA_HOST` from the environment (defaults to `http://localhost:11434`).\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- `model` - Model name (e.g. `\"llama3\"`, `\"mistral:7b\"`)\n\n### `createOllamaChat(model, hostOrConfig?)`\n\nCreates an Ollama text/chat adapter with an explicit host or client config.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- `model` - Model name\n- `hostOrConfig?` - Either an `OLLAMA_HOST`-style URL string, or an `OllamaClientConfig` object (e.g. `{ baseURL, defaultHeaders }`). `host` and `headers` are aliases.\n\n### `ollamaSummarize(model)` / `createOllamaSummarize(model, hostOrConfig?)`\n\nCreates an Ollama summarization adapter — same signature shape as the chat adapter.\n\n## Benefits of Ollama\n\n- ✅ **Privacy** - Data stays on your infrastructure\n- ✅ **Cost** - No API costs after hardware\n- ✅ **Customization** - Use any compatible model\n- ✅ **Offline** - Works without internet\n- ✅ **Speed** - No network latency for local deployment\n\n## Limitations\n\n- **Image Generation**: Ollama does not support image generation. Use OpenAI or Gemini for image generation.\n- **Performance**: Depends on your hardware (GPU recommended for larger models)\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Getting Started](../getting-started/quick-start) - Learn the basics\n- [Tools Guide](../tools/tools) - Learn about tools\n- [Other Adapters](./openai) - Explore other providers\n"}
